<Rung Number="140" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[BARE WIRE ROTATION AND RETRY COUNTERS

The wire will be inspected and then rotated 90 degrees,
therefore Counter[0].PRE is set to (4) to keep track of rotations

Counter[2] is used for retrying the vision inspection after a FAIL]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Status.State[22])ONS(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.OS[3])[MOVE(HMI_Data.Control.DINT_SP[5],Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].PRE) CTU(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0],?,?) ,MOVE(HMI_Data.Control.DINT_SP[6],Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[2].PRE) CTU(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[2],?,?) ]MOVE(0,Pointer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="141" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Evaluate Pointer for BARE WIRE Inspection

Counter[0] is for keeping track of wire rotations

Counter[2] is for multiple inspection attempts (intially 2) 
enabling a re-trigger of the camera if the inspection fails

The 'Pointer' controls where the program 'goes next':
[22] Re-trigger the camera                                     
[24] Rotate the wire for the next inspeection angle   
or [26] Retract from the camera, all inspections complete]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Status.State[53])XIC(Vision_SM.Status.State[7])[MOVE(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].ACC,n) ,XIC(in_WireData[0].StripInspect_RESULTS[n].Inspect_FAIL) XIO(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[2].DN) ONS(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.OS[10]) SUB(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].ACC,1,Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].ACC) MOVE(22,Pointer) ,[XIC(in_WireData[0].StripInspect_RESULTS[n].Inspect_PASS) ,XIC(in_WireData[0].StripInspect_RESULTS[n].Inspect_FAIL) XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[2].DN) ] [XIO(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].DN) RES(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[2]) MOVE(24,Pointer) ,XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].DN) MOVE(26,Pointer) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="142" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[TINNED WIRE ROTATION AND RETRY COUNTER

The wire will be inspected and then rotated 90 degrees,
therefore Counter[2].PRE is set to (4) to keep track of rotations

Counter[3] is used for retrying the vision inspection after a FAIL]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Status.State[32])ONS(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.OS[4])[MOVE(HMI_Data.Control.DINT_SP[5],Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[1].PRE) CTU(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[1],?,?) ,MOVE(HMI_Data.Control.DINT_SP[6],Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[3].PRE) CTU(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[3],?,?) ]MOVE(0,Pointer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="143" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Evaluate Pointer for TINNED WIRE Inspection

Counter[1] is for keeping track of wire rotations

Counter[3] is for multiple inspection attempts (intially 2) 
enabling a re-trigger of the camera if the inspection fails

The 'Pointer' controls where the program 'goes next':
[32] Re-trigger the camera                                     
[34] Rotate the wire for the next inspeection angle   
or [36] Retract from the camera, all inspections complete]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Status.State[55])XIC(Vision_SM.Status.State[7])[MOVE(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[1].ACC,n) ,XIC(in_WireData[0].TinningInspect_RESULTS[n].Inspect_FAIL) XIO(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[3].DN) ONS(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.OS[11]) SUB(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[1].ACC,1,Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[1].ACC) MOVE(32,Pointer) ,[XIC(in_WireData[0].TinningInspect_RESULTS[n].Inspect_PASS) ,XIC(in_WireData[0].TinningInspect_RESULTS[n].Inspect_FAIL) XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[3].DN) ] [XIO(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[1].DN) RES(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[3]) MOVE(34,Pointer) ,XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[1].DN) MOVE(36,Pointer) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="144" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[NE(EDA.in.R60,5)OTE(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Bit[6]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="145" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(RobotStatus.UserIn2.6)OTE(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Bit[7]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="146" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Status.State[46])TON(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Timer[9],?,?)XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Timer[9].DN)ONS(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.OS[7])OTE(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Bit[13]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="147" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Robot01_Wire_SM.Status.State[46])OTE(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Bit[8]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="148" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SUB(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].PRE,1,TriggerValue)EQ(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Counter[0].ACC,TriggerValue)OTE(Robot01_Wire_SM.Control.Bit[12]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
